Nginx 1.3.9 predates libxcrypt (Ubuntu >= 20.04), whose struct crypt_data has no
current_salt member. The line only pre-initialised a glibc-internal field; crypt_r()
does not need it. Same fix as later Nginx releases.
--- a/src/os/unix/ngx_user.c
+++ b/src/os/unix/ngx_user.c
@@ -35,7 +35,6 @@ ngx_libc_crypt(ngx_pool_t *pool, u_char *key, u_char *salt, u_char **encrypted)
     struct crypt_data   cd;
 
     cd.initialized = 0;
-    /* work around the glibc bug */
-    cd.current_salt[0] = ~salt[0];
+    /* glibc workaround removed: libxcrypt's crypt_data has no current_salt */
 
     value = crypt_r((char *) key, (char *) salt, &cd);
